description:
In `rust/lichen-schc/src/fragment.rs`, the `std_ext::FragmentReceiver::new(window_size: usize)` accepts any `usize` without validating it against 64 (the width of `u64` used in `window_bitmap`). The method:

```rust
fn window_bitmap(&self, abs_window: usize) -> u64 {
    let base = abs_window * self.window_size;
    let mut bitmap: u64 = 0;
    for p in 0..self.window_size {
        if self.tiles.contains_key(&(base + p)) {
            bitmap |= 1u64 << (self.window_size - 1 - p);
        }
    }
    bitmap
}
```

If `self.window_size > 64`, the shift `1u64 << (self.window_size - 1 - 0)` shifts by >= 64 bits, which is undefined behavior in Rust (panic in debug, UB in release).

Additionally, `Ack::new` masks with `BITMAP_MASK = (1 << 32) - 1`, so even for window sizes 33–62 (which would not trigger UB), the bitmap bits beyond position 31 would be silently truncated, producing an incorrect acknowledgment.

**Fix**: Add `debug_assert!(window_size <= MAX_WINDOW_SIZE)` or `debug_assert!(window_size <= 64)` to `FragmentReceiver::new`. Also consider whether `MAX_WINDOW_SIZE` should be used consistently instead of the hardcoded 64 bound (for future-proofing the bitmap width).

